Main Group ‑ level governance bodies have the following roles:

the General Management Doubtful Committee (CDDG) is the Group’s highest level decision ‑ making committee in terms of specific provisioning and recognitions of losses relative to the Group’s customer exposures;

the Financial Markets Risk Committee (FMRC) is the body which governs the Group’s risk profile of the capital markets activities; its tasks include, among others, analysing market and counterparty risks and setting limits for capital markets activities;

Capital Committee, described under Capital management in section 5.2 Capital management and capital adequacy , validates the Group’s objectives in terms of solvency ratios and Total Loss Absorbing Capacity (TLAC and MREL) requirements in case of resolution as well as the trajectory to achieve these targets, monitors the compliance with this trajectory and, when relevant, proposes corrective actions to achieve target solvency ratios. As the Group’s competent Executive Management authority for all issues related to the internal credit and operational risks model, the Capital Committee is informed of decisions made in the MARCo Committees (Model Approval and Review Committee);

the Risk & Development Policy Committees (RDPC) have the dual objective of defining an appropriate risk policy for any given subject which may be a business activity, a product, a geographic area (region or country), a customer segment or economic sector, and of investigating development opportunities in relation to the subject in question;

Group ALM Treasury Committee (Group ALCo) is responsible for the management of the liquidity risk, interest rate risk in the banking book and structural foreign exchange risk over the whole Group;

the Country Strategic RDPCs define the Group’s risk appetite by setting country envelopes for medium ‑ to ‑ high ‑ risk countries considering country risk, market conditions, business strategies as well as other topics such as those related to compliance or climate risk;

Group Supervision and Control Committee (GSCC) brings together the Group’s control functions at Executive Management level and takes a Group ‑ wide approach to tackling all aspects of non financial risk exposure;

the Group Artificial Intelligence (AI) committee (GAIC) oversees the development and approval of the Group's AI Strategy, and manages its implementation and operational deployment across the Group. The missions of the GAIC are:

